 https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C1735870</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Naprapathy</rdfs:label>
        <core:altLabel>Naprapathic Medicine</core:altLabel>
        <UMLS_CUI>C1735870</UMLS_CUI>
        <UMLS_Semantic_Type>Therapeutic or Preventive Procedure</UMLS_Semantic_Type>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000022 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000022">
        <rdfs:comment>Source: Medical Subject Headings (MeSH)
 http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/MESH/D000529</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: National Cancer Institute Thesaurus (NCIT)
 http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C15178</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: Physician Data Query (PDQ) Terminology
 http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/PDQ/CDR0000042022</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: Read Clinical Terminology Version 2 (RCTV2)
  http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RCTV2/8BF..00</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: Read Codes, Clinical Terms Version 3 (CTV3)
  http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RCD/Ua1Ty</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: UMLS 
 https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C1148474</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Complementary_Medicine_Intervention</rdfs:label>
        <core:altLabel>Alternative Medicine</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Alternative Therapies</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>CAM</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>CAM procedure</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>CAM therapy</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Complementary Medicine</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Complementary Therapies</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Complementary Therapy</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Complementary and Integrative Health</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Complementary therapy</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>complementary and alternative medicine</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>complementary or alternative medical therapy</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>complementary or alternative medicine procedure</core:altLabel>
        <core:definition>[Source: Medical Subject Headings (MeSH)] Therapeutic practices which are not currently considered an integral part of conventional allopathic medical practice. They may lack biomedical explanations but as they become better researched some (PHYSICAL THERAPY MODALITIES; DIET; ACUPUNCTURE) become widely accepted whereas others (humors, radium therapy) quietly fade away, yet are important historical footnotes. Therapies are termed as Complementary when used in addition to conventional treatments and as Alternative when used instead of conventional treatment. Therapies are termed as Alternative when used instead of conventional treatment.</core:definition>
        <core:definition>[Source: National Cancer Institute Thesaurus (NCIT)] A group of diverse medical and health care systems, practices, and products that are not presently considered to be part of conventional medicine. Complementary medicine as being used together with conventional medicine, whereas alternative medicine is used in place of conventional medicine. The National Center for Complementary and Alternative Medicine (NCCAM) groups CAM practices into four domains, recognizing there can be some overlap: mind-body medicine; biologically based practices, manipulative and body-based practices, and energy medicine. In addition, NCCAM studies CAM whole medical systems, which cut across all domains.</core:definition>
        <UMLS_CUI>C1148474</UMLS_CUI>
        <UMLS_Semantic_Type>Biomedical Occupation or Discipline</UMLS_Semantic_Type>
    </owl:Class>
    


