    <!-- https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000144 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000144">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000135"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: CIHLex</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: Medical Subject Headings (MeSH)
 http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/MESH/D001676</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: Physician Data Query (PDQ) Terminology
 http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/PDQ/CDR0000574223</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: UMLS 
 https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C0005491</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Biofeedback</rdfs:label>
        <core:altLabel>Biofeedback (Psychology)</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Biofeedback Therapy</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Biofeedback Training</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Biofeedbacks (Psychology)</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Bogus Physiological Feedback</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Bogus Physiological Feedbacks</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>False Physiological Feedback</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>False Physiological Feedbacks</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Myofeedback</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Myofeedbacks</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Psychology Biofeedback</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Psychology Biofeedbacks</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Psychophysiologic Feedback</core:altLabel>
        <core:definition>Assisting the patient to gain voluntary control over physiological responses using feedback from electronic equipment that monitors physiologic processes (NIC)</core:definition>
        <core:definition>Provision of immediate ongoing information regarding one&apos;s own physiological processes. (PSY)</core:definition>
        <core:definition>The therapy technique of providing the status of one&apos;s own AUTONOMIC NERVOUS SYSTEM function (e.g., skin temperature, heartbeats, brain waves) as visual or auditory feedback in order to self-control related conditions (e.g., hypertension, migraine headaches). (MSH)</core:definition>
        <core:definition>Using a biofeedback monitoring device or galvanic skin response on a client to assess his or her physical response to indicate an emotional problem. Service is billed per session. (ALT)</core:definition>
        <core:definition>[Source: Medical Subject Headings (MeSH)] The therapy technique of providing the status of one&apos;s own AUTONOMIC NERVOUS SYSTEM function (e.g., skin temperature, heartbeats, brain waves) as visual or auditory feedback in order to self-control related conditions (e.g., hypertension, migraine headaches).</core:definition>
        <core:definition>[Source: Physician Data Query (PDQ)] Biofeedback is a training technique in which people are taught to improve their health and performance by using signals from their own bodies. (AAPB) Check for &quot;https://www.cancer.gov/about-cancer/treatment/clinical-trials/intervention/C15186&quot; active clinical trials using this agent. (&quot;http://ncit.nci.nih.gov/ncitbrowser/ConceptReport.jsp?dictionary=NCI%20Thesaurus&amp;code=C15186&quot; NCI Thesaurus)</core:definition>
        <core:definition>feedback loop consists of an organism, its response, and a method of detecting and displaying the response. (CSP)</core:definition>
        <UMLS_CUI>C0005491</UMLS_CUI>
        <UMLS_Semantic_Type>Therapeutic or Preventive Procedure</UMLS_Semantic_Type>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000145 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000145">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000144"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: Medical Subject Headings (MeSH)
 http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/MESH/D056228</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: UMLS 
 https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C0178842</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Sensory_Feedback</rdfs:label>
        <core:altLabel>Audio Feedback</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Audio Feedbacks</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Proprioceptive Feedback</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Proprioceptive Feedbacks</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Sensorimotor Feedback</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Sensorimotor Feedbacks</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Sensory Feedback</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Sensory Feedbacks</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Visual Feedback</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Visual Feedbacks</core:altLabel>
        <core:definition>Return of afferent neural signals or information from sensory receptors. Sensory feedback may function in the regulation of behavior in general but is especially important in the control of bodily movement. Use a more specific term if possible. (PSY)</core:definition>
        <core:definition>[Source: Medical Subject Headings (MeSH)] A mechanism of communicating one&apos;s own sensory system information about a task, movement or skill.</core:definition>
        <core:definition>a mechanism of communication within the sensory system in that the input signal generates an output response which returns to influence the continued activity or productivity of the sensory system. (CSP)</core:definition>
        <UMLS_CUI>C0178842</UMLS_CUI>
        <UMLS_Semantic_Type>Mental Process</UMLS_Semantic_Type>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000146 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000146">
