    <!-- https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000213 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000213">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000212"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: CIHLex</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: Physician Data Query (PDQ) Terminology
 http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/PDQ/CDR0000574167</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: UMLS 
 https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C1511139</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Biofield_Therapy</rdfs:label>
        <core:altLabel>Bioenergy Healing</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Biofield Energy Therapy</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Biofield Medicine</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>Biofields</core:altLabel>
        <core:definition>[Source: Physician Data Query (PDQ) Terminology] A form of therapy which involves systems that use &quot;subtle energy&quot; fields in and around the body for medical purposes. Examples include Therapeutic Touch, Reiki, Hunna, laying-on-of-hands, external Qi-Gong, etc. Included are: Therapeutic Touch, Healing Science, Healing touch, Natural healing, SHEN, Mariuel, Reiki, Huna, External QiGong, Biorelax. Check for &quot;https://www.cancer.gov/about-cancer/treatment/clinical-trials/intervention/C15910&quot; active clinical trials using this agent. (&quot;http://ncit.nci.nih.gov/ncitbrowser/ConceptReport.jsp?dictionary=NCI%20Thesaurus&amp;code=C15910&quot; NCI Thesaurus)</core:definition>
        <UMLS_CUI>C1511139</UMLS_CUI>
        <UMLS_Semantic_Type>Therapeutic or Preventive Procedure</UMLS_Semantic_Type>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000214 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000214">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000213"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: CIHLex</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: National Center for Complementary and Integrative Health (NCCIH)
 https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/reiki</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: Natural Medicine</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: Physician Data Query (PDQ) Terminology
 http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/PDQ/CDR0000574168</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: Read Clinical Terminology Version 2 (RCTV2) http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RCTV2/8BF5.00</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: UMLS 
 https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C0751715</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Reiki_Therapy</rdfs:label>
        <core:altLabel>Reiki</core:altLabel>
        <core:definition>A biofield therapy that relies upon a belief in an invisible energy that may be transmitted from healer to patient through intention. (SNOMEDCT_US)</core:definition>
        <core:definition>Using a specific sequence of hand positions and symbols to channel the universal life force for recharging, realigning, and rebalancing the human energy field (NIC)</core:definition>
        <core:definition>Using an energetic healing technique to facilitate a connection with a client&apos;s life-force energy to reduce his or her stress, and/or enhance relaxation and/or wellbeing. Any practitioner using this code must document appropriate training and/or certification. Service is billed in 15-minute increments. (ALT)</core:definition>
        <core:definition>[Source: National Center for Complementary and Integrative Health (NCCIH)] Reiki is a complementary health approach in which practitioners place their hands lightly on or just above a person, with the goal of directing energy to help facilitate the person’s own healing response. It’s based on an Eastern belief in an energy that supports the body’s innate or natural healing abilities.</core:definition>
        <core:definition>[Source: Physician Data Query (PDQ) Terminology] An alternative medical practice. The practitioners of reiki believe that health and disease are a matter of the life force being disrupted. Reiki healers claim to channel reiki into &quot;diseased&quot; individuals for &quot;rebalancing.&quot; (from Skeptic&apos;s Dictionary) Check for &quot;https://www.cancer.gov/about-cancer/treatment/clinical-trials/intervention/C15728&quot; active clinical trials using this agent. (&quot;http://ncit.nci.nih.gov/ncitbrowser/ConceptReport.jsp?dictionary=NCI%20Thesaurus&amp;code=C15728&quot; NCI Thesaurus)</core:definition>
        <UMLS_CUI>C0751715</UMLS_CUI>
        <UMLS_Semantic_Type>Therapeutic or Preventive Procedure</UMLS_Semantic_Type>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000215 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000215">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000214"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: CIHLex</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: Natural Medicine</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Japanese_Reiki</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000216 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000216">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000214"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: CIHLex</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: Natural Medicine</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Buddhist_Reiki</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000217 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000217">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000213"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: Medical Subject Headings (MeSH)
 http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/MESH/D019124</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: Physician Data Query (PDQ) Terminology
 http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/PDQ/CDR0000470290</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: UMLS 
 https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C0152054</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Therapeutic_Touch</rdfs:label>
        <core:altLabel>Laying-on-of-Hands</core:altLabel>
        <core:definition>An energy (biofield) therapy that encompasses a group of non-invasive techniques that utilize the hands to clear, energize, and balance the human and environmental energy fields. Healing Touch interventions may be used to restore, energize, and balance an energy field disturbance. (HTA) (NCI)</core:definition>
        <core:definition>Attuning to the universal energy field by seeking to act as a healing influence using the natural sensitivity of hands and passing them over the body to gently focus, direct, and modulate the human energy field. Providing comfort and communication through purposeful tactile contact . Providing a noninvasive, biofield therapy using touch and compassionate intentionality to influence the energy system of a person, affecting their physical, emotional, mental, and spiritual health and healing (NIC)</core:definition>
        <core:definition>Directing an intentional process of energy exchange with a client to facilitate and/or promote his or her healing process. Any practitioner using this code must document appropriate training and/or certification. Service is billed in 15-minute increments. (ALT)</core:definition>
        <core:definition>[Source: Medical Subject Headings (MeSH)] Placing of the hands of the healer upon the person to be cured with the intent of spiritual energetic healing.</core:definition>
        <UMLS_CUI>C0152054</UMLS_CUI>
        <UMLS_Semantic_Type>Therapeutic or Preventive Procedure</UMLS_Semantic_Type>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000218 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000218">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://github.com/Tao-AI-group/COMBINI#000213"/>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: CIHLex</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: NCCIH</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: UMLS 
 https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C1160821</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>[Source: Natural Medicines] 
 https://naturalmedicines.therapeuticresearch.com/databases/health-wellness/professional.aspx?productid=1448</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Healing_Touch</rdfs:label>
        <UMLS_CUI>C1160821</UMLS_CUI>
