 https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C3899490</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Cranial_Electrical_Stimulation</rdfs:label>
        <core:altLabel>CES</core:altLabel>
        <core:definition>The use of skin electrodes to pass a low intensity, pulsed electrical current through the scalp and into the brain. This procedure is used to treat a variety of illnesses including anxiety, depression, and chronic pain. (NCI)</core:definition>
