 https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C0695601</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Myotherapy</rdfs:label>
        <core:definition>Using myotherapy, which consists of applying pressure from origin to insertion of a client&apos;s muscle(s), to release tension at the point(s) of attachment between his or her muscle(s) and bone(s). Any practitioner using this code must document appropriate training and/or certification. Service is billed in 15-minute increments. (ALT)</core:definition>
        <UMLS_CUI>C0695601</UMLS_CUI>
        <UMLS_Semantic_Type>Therapeutic or Preventive Procedure</UMLS_Semantic_Type>
