        <rdfs:comment>Source: CIHLex</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source: Natural Medicine</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Source:UMLS 
 https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C0454416</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Hippotherapy</rdfs:label>
        <core:definition>A treatment strategy that uses the movement of the horse as a treatment tool for the rider who has physical, developmental or other limitations (e.g., cerebral palsy). Typically, a hippotherapy session involves a team of a health professional (e.g., occupational therapist), a horse handler, and the rider. The rhythm of the horse&apos;s movement is thought to challenge and influence the rider in improving balance, muscle symmetry, gross motor functions, etc. (MSH)</core:definition>
        <UMLS_CUI>C0454416</UMLS_CUI>
        <UMLS_Semantic_Type>Therapeutic or Preventive Procedure</UMLS_Semantic_Type>
    </owl:Class>
    


