        <core:altLabel>Clown Therapy</core:altLabel>
        <core:definition>[Source: Medical Subject Headings (MeSH)] A form of exercise involving use of laughter and breathing exercises in order to improve physical and mental health. Therapeutic use of humor and laughter to improve emotional well being and health. Healthcare provider use of clown or other comedic image or costumes to reduce patient anxiety or fear.</core:definition>
