 https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C0679661</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Suggestion_Therapy</rdfs:label>
        <core:definition>suggestion thearpy is a type of psychotherapy in which distressing symptoms are alleviated by direct suggestion and reassurance. The technique is sometimes used in hypnotherapy. A suggestion may be accompanied by an explanation of the meaning and the purpose of the symptoms, but no attempt is made to modify the client’s basic personality. (APA dictionary of psychology: https://dictionary.apa.org/suggestion-therapy)</core:definition>
        <UMLS_CUI>C0679661</UMLS_CUI>
        <UMLS_Semantic_Type>Therapeutic or Preventive Procedure</UMLS_Semantic_Type>
    </owl:Class>
    


