 https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/goldenseal</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Goldenseal</rdfs:label>
        <core:altLabel>goldenroot</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>yellow pucoon</core:altLabel>
        <core:altLabel>yellow root</core:altLabel>
        <core:definition>[Source: National Center for Complementary and Integrative Health (NCCIH)] Goldenseal is a plant native to the northeastern United States and southeastern Canada. It has a bright yellow rhizome (underground stem). Wild goldenseal has been overharvested and is available in limited amounts. The plant is grown commercially but is expensive to cultivate.</core:definition>
    </owl:Class>
    


